            <ArticleTitle>What Role Does Allergy Play in Chronic Ear Disease and Laryngitis?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>76</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>IgE-mediated allergy plays a well-established role in both nasal and pulmonary diseases due to the common epithelium and shared mediator responses of the upper and lower airways. This &quot;unified airway&quot; concept has also been described in other sites within the head and neck that contain similar respiratory mucosa: the middle ear and the larynx. This review will highlight the data suggesting a role for IgE-mediated allergic disease in chronic laryngopharyngeal and middle ear disease and the role for allergy testing to aid in diagnosis and treatment of these disorders.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
